  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1109 PM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nMostly clear skies and dry conditions are expected today with lows \nlight and variable winds. Lows this morning will dip into the low \n40s with highs this afternoon in the mid to upper 60s. A weak cold \nfront will move through after midnight tonight shifting winds to the \nnorth with an increase in speed. No precipitation is expected with \nan increase in mid to upper level cloudiness. Skies return to being \nmostly clear by tomorrow afternoon into tomorrow night. Lows tonight \nwill dip into the low to mid 40s with highs tomorrow in the mid to \nupper 60s. Dry conditions are then expected through Saturday. Mid \nrange models show a chance of precipitation Saturday night into \nSunday as a disturbance moves through the area. But confidence is \nlow that this will occur. We then return dry for the remainder of \nthe forecast. As for temperatures, Highs Thursday will range from \nthe upper 50s across north central Kansas to upper 60s across far \nsouthwestern Kansas. Highs only reach into the 50s to low 60s Friday \nbefore reaching to around 60 degrees this weekend into the early \npart of next week.",
